# Session 62 Phase 3a: realistic cost_cap example with souls + bounds.
#
# Demonstrates the four cost-related declarations:
#
#   1. cost_cap: <amount> <currency>      (per world)
#   2. max_ticks: <integer>               (per world)
#   3. mind: <model> @ <tier>             (per soul)
#   4. tokens: input=<N> output=<M>       (per soul)
#
# Souls are top-level entities, sibling to the world. The world's
# cost_cap aggregates the cost of all souls operating under it,
# bounded by max_ticks heartbeat cycles.
#
# `instinct` blocks (the per-tick agent logic) are intentionally
# omitted here to keep the example focused on cost declarations.
# See templates/customer_service.nous for `instinct` examples.

world TradingFloor {
    cost_cap: 0.50 USD
    max_ticks: 5
}

soul Trader {
    mind: claude-opus-4-7 @ Tier1
    tokens: input=500 output=200
}

soul Analyst {
    mind: claude-haiku-4-5 @ Tier3
    tokens: input=300 output=150
}
